1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,580
Tooth decay starts before a hole. What tips the balance?

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:13,143
Some bacteria in plaque use sugars to make acids. Repeated exposure can keep enamel losing minerals.

3
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:22,211
Saliva and fluoride help replace lost minerals. Early decay can sometimes be stopped or reversed before a cavity forms.

4
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:30,587
If loss keeps winning, the surface can break down. A formed cavity needs dental assessment and appropriate treatment.

5
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:38,573
A dentist assesses the tooth and selects treatment. A filling is one common way to restore damaged structure.

6
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:47,402
The long game is prevention: fluoride toothpaste twice daily, cleaning between teeth, and regular dental review.
